{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2jbf6tdfGKxZgmnzVsX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed. Summary:\n\n- `attavo/store.py::put` now accepts an optional `at` param (defaults to reading the clock, unchanged for other callers like `counsel.py`).\n- `attavo/plan.py::set_claims` now takes `at` as a parameter instead of calling `now_iso()` itself.\n- `cmd_plan`'s `claims` verb reads the clock once and passes that single stamp to both `set_claims` and the `store.put` write, so the claim's `at` and the store version's `at` agree by construction.\n- Added the rejection test from the spec's stub (`test_a_plan_write_stamps_the_claim_and_the_version_from_one_clock_read`) to `tests/test_plan.py`.\n\nTests for the affected files (`tests/test_plan.py`, `tests/test_store.py`) pass — 34/34. The one failure from the full `attavo test 339` run (`test_testtool.py::test_attavo_test_ends_a_run_past_its_bound_with_everything_it_started`) is a pre-existing sandbox limitation (the sandbox blocks `ps`), confirmed by reproducing it on the unmodified tree before making changes — unrelated to this fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_read_input_tokens":67916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":369},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eecc161-6573-44a2-80b2-9b0f791072cd","uuid":"7aba7136-7e1f-4082-a806-04b7f1e73db8","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:09:09.109Z","request_id":"req_011Cg2jbesW5UQkJHXk4Em6j"}
